Appendix G: Oxia Planum Falsifiability Formalization

G.1 Setup

Let T_{\text{cut}} = 2018\text{-}01\text{-}01.

Define:

\mathcal{E}_{T}(r) = \{e \in \mathcal{E}(r) : \text{timestamp}(e) < T_{\text{cut}}\},

\mathcal{L}_{T} = \{p \in \mathcal{L} : \text{timestamp}(p) < T_{\text{cut}}\}.

Apply the two-stage filter (Appendix F) to obtain \mathcal{L}_{T}(r).

G.2 Region Set

Let R_{50} be the set of all tiles r such that:

\text{dist}(r, \text{Oxia\_center}) \leq 50 \text{ km}.

G.3 Ranking

Compute S_{\text{contradiction}}(r) for all r \in R_{50} using \mathcal{E}_{T}(r) and \mathcal{L}_{T}(r).

Rank all r \in R_{50} by S_{\text{contradiction}}(r) in descending order. Let \text{CSAZ}_{5\%} be the top 5% of this ranking.

G.4 Falsification Condition

Let r_{\text{Xiong}} be the study region of Xiong et al. (2023).

H4 is falsified iff:

r_{\text{Xiong}} \notin \text{CSAZ}_{5\%}.

G.5 Why This Is Falsifiable

The condition is a single, pre-registered, binary test. It does not depend on post-hoc choice of k. The 5% threshold and 50 km radius are fixed in advance. If EIM fails this test, H4 is falsified regardless of other results.

