Appendix H: Evaluation Metrics Formalization

H.1 Precision@k

Let \text{Top}_k be the top k regions by S_{\text{final}}(r). Let \mathcal{R} be the set of regions with human rating \geq 4 on the "priority for follow-up inspection" scale.

\text{Precision@k} = \frac{|\text{Top}_k \cap \mathcal{R}|}{k}.

H.2 NDCG@k

Let \text{rel}_i be the human rating (1–5) of the region at rank i.

\text{DCG@k} = \sum_{i=1}^k \frac{2^{\text{rel}_i} - 1}{\log_2(i+1)},

\text{IDCG@k} = \sum_{i=1}^k \frac{2^{\text{rel}_i^{\text{ideal}}} - 1}{\log_2(i+1)},

where \text{rel}_i^{\text{ideal}} is the i-th largest relevance in the full set.

\text{NDCG@k} = \frac{\text{DCG@k}}{\text{IDCG@k}}.

H.3 AUC

Let \mathcal{P} be the set of positive regions (rating \geq 4) and \mathcal{N} be the set of negative regions (rating \leq 2).

\text{AUC} = \frac{1}{|\mathcal{P}| \cdot |\mathcal{N}|} \sum_{i \in \mathcal{P}} \sum_{j \in \mathcal{N}} \psi(S_{\text{final}}(i), S_{\text{final}}(j)),

where

\psi(a, b) = \begin{cases}
1, & a > b, \\
0.5, & a = b, \\
0, & a < b.
\end{cases}

H.4 Inter-Rater Agreement

Quadratic-weighted Cohen's \kappa:

\kappa_w = 1 - \frac{\sum_{i,j} w_{ij} O_{ij}}{\sum_{i,j} w_{ij} E_{ij}},

where O_{ij} is the observed agreement matrix, E_{ij} is the expected agreement matrix under independence, and

w_{ij} = 1 - \left(\frac{i - j}{K - 1}\right)^2

for a K-point Likert scale.

ICC(2,k):

\text{ICC}(2,k) = \frac{\text{MS}_R - \text{MS}_E}{\text{MS}_R + (k-1)\text{MS}_E + \frac{k}{n}(\text{MS}_C - \text{MS}_E)},

where \text{MS}_R is the mean square for rows (subjects), \text{MS}_C is the mean square for columns (raters), \text{MS}_E is the mean square error, n is the number of subjects, and k is the number of raters.

