   │     (e.g., thermal inertia vs. albedo)                                  │
   │     → EXCLUDED from both V_A and V_D                                    │
   │     → not comparable, not a scientific discrepancy                      │
   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   FAILURE MODE PREVENTED:
   ──────────────────────
   Without R(r) as first-class variable, a 100 m horizontal offset between
   two HiRISE DTMs can generate a spurious "subsurface reflector" in a
   SHARAD-DTM comparison — exactly the artifact class that Xiong et al.
   (2023) identified as clutter. EIM blocks this by requiring R_ij > 0.5
   before computing D(r). Regions failing all pairs report status
   "unverifiable" rather than a numeric discrepancy score.
